{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"f1c61a298ccf44badcd26aad2cb565609b6b89d14433f3e766d2e9b8550f4f34","packTokens":4393,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":41,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":4331,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"State, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The maintenance request system shall provide a browser-accessible web front end, an HTTP API, and a database that stores request records.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The application and database are running. when A client creates a request through the HTTP API and retrieves it by its returned ID. then The database row and response record contain the same generated ID and request field values.\",\n    \"Given The application is running. when A user opens the application in a browser. then The Requests screen is displayed.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an empty database is initialized, the maintenance request system shall seed exactly eight requests: four Open including exactly one Urgent, two In progress, and two Done, with every supported area represented.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The database is empty before first initialization. when The application initializes and a client lists all requests through the API. then The response list has a count of 8, with status counts of 4 Open, 2 In progress, and 2 Done; exactly one Open request has Urgent priority, and the list includes every supported area.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The maintenance request system shall persist request records across browser reloads and application restarts.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A request has been created and its ID recorded. when The application service is restarted and a client retrieves that ID through the API. then The response record contains the created request's ID and field values.\",\n    \"Given A request is visible in the Requests list. when The browser page is reloaded. then The screen shows the persisted request row.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The API shall expose exactly four request operations and no others: list requests, create a request, get a request by ID, and change a request's status.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API is available. when A client invokes list, create, get by ID, and change status using HTTP calls. then Each call returns a response for its corresponding request operation.\",\n    \"Given A request exists and its current record has been retrieved. when A client attempts to edit a fixed request field or delete the request through the API. then Each call returns an error response and the request record remains unchanged.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a client lists requests, the API shall return all requests or only requests matching one requested status, ordered newest first.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Requests with different statuses and creation times exist. when A client lists requests without a status and then lists requests with one status filter. then The first response list contains all requests newest first, and the filtered response list contains only matching statuses newest first.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a client creates a valid request, the maintenance request system shall assign an ID and UTC creation time and set its status to Open.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A client has valid request fields. when The client creates a request through the API. then The response record contains a system-generated ID, a UTC creation time, and status Open.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a client submits a request for creation, the maintenance request system shall require a title trimmed to 3 to 80 characters, an area of Kitchen, Meeting room, Open desk, Washroom, or Reception, a priority of Low, Normal, or Urgent, and an optional description of at most 500 characters, rejecting invalid values with an error naming the field.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A client submits requests with a missing title, a two-character title, a title over 80 characters, a missing or unsupported area, a missing or unsupported priority, or a description over 500 characters. when The client sends each request to the create API operation. then Each invalid response contains an error naming the invalid field, and the two-character title response contains “Title must be 3 to 80 characters.”\",\n    \"Given A client submits a title with surrounding whitespace that leaves 3 to 80 characters after trimming, and a title containing only whitespace in a separate request. when The client creates both requests through the API. then The valid response record contains the trimmed title, and the invalid response contains a Title error.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The API shall keep title, area, priority, and description fixed after creation and reject attempts to change those fields or delete a request.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A request exists with known title, area, priority, and description values. when A client attempts to change each of those fields or delete the request through the API. then The response is an error and the retrieved record retains its original field values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The maintenance request API shall accept the transitions Open to In progress, In progress to Done, and Done to Open and reject all other status changes; a status change for an unknown request ID shall return a not-found response, and a missing status body or unrecognized status value shall return an error without changing any request.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A request has status Open. when A client changes its status to In progress through the API. then The response record has status In progress.\",\n    \"Given A request has status In progress. when A client changes its status to Done through the API. then The response record has status Done.\",\n    \"Given A request has status Done. when A client changes its status to Open through the API. then The response record has status Open.\",\n    \"Given A request has status Open. when A client attempts to change its status directly to Done. then The response is an error and the retrieved record still has status Open.\",\n    \"Given No request has the ID supplied to the status-change operation. when A client attempts to change status for that ID through the API. then The response identifies the request as not found.\",\n    \"Given A request exists and its current record has been retrieved. when A client sends a status-change request with no body. then The response is an error and the request row retains its original status.\",\n    \"Given A request exists and its current record has been retrieved. when A client sends a status-change request with an unrecognized status value. then The response is an error and the request row retains its original status.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Requests screen shall display the Hive Works wordmark, the signed-in demo user's initials SC, a status filter with All, Open, In progress, and Done choices with All selected initially, a New request button, and a newest-first request list.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The Requests screen has loaded. when A user views the screen before changing any filter. then The screen displays the Hive Works wordmark, SC, the four filter choices with All selected, the New request button, and the request list.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a user selects a status filter or returns from request detail, the Requests screen shall load the list for the selected filter and retain that filter on return from detail.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The Requests screen is showing a selected status filter. when The user opens a request detail screen, changes its status successfully, and returns to the Requests screen. then The screen retains the selected filter and displays a refreshed list in which a request that no longer matches may be absent.\",\n    \"Given The Requests screen is loaded. when The user selects a status filter. then The screen displays the refreshed list for that filter.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the user opens New request, the Requests screen shall show a dialog with Title, Area, Priority defaulting to Normal, and Description fields, plus Create and Cancel controls.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The Requests screen is displayed. when The user activates New request. then The screen shows a dialog with labeled Title, Area, Priority, and Description fields, Normal selected for Priority, and Create and Cancel controls.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When valid request creation succeeds, the Requests screen shall close the dialog, select All, and show the new Open request at the top of the list.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The create dialog is open and a filter other than All is selected. when The user submits valid request fields and the create API call succeeds. then The screen closes the dialog, selects All, and shows the new Open request row at the top of the list.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a create field fails validation, the Requests screen shall keep the dialog open and display the field's error message under that field.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The create dialog is open. when The user submits a title of two characters. then The screen keeps the dialog open and displays “Title must be 3 to 80 characters.” under the Title field.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the create API call fails for a reason other than field validation, the Requests screen shall show “Could not create request.” in the dialog, retain entered values, and allow retry.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The create dialog contains entered values. when The create API call fails for a non-validation reason. then The screen displays “Could not create request.” in the dialog, retains the entered field values, and shows an enabled retry path through Create.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"While requests are loading, absent for the selected filter, or fail to load, the Requests screen shall display the corresponding loading, empty, or error state with retry available for load errors.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The Requests list request is in progress. when The user views the Requests screen. then The screen displays “Loading requests…”.\",\n    \"Given No requests match the selected filter. when The Requests screen finishes loading the list. then The screen displays “No requests here.”\",\n    \"Given The list API call fails. when The Requests screen handles the failure. then The screen displays “Could not load requests.” and a Retry button.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a request exists, the request detail screen shall display a back link, its title, area, priority badge, status badge, created date, and description or “No description.” when the description is empty.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A request with a description and a request without a description both exist. when The user opens each request detail screen. then Each screen displays the request fields, badges, created date, and back link, and the screen for the request without a description displays “No description.”\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The request detail screen shall show Start work for Open, Mark done for In progress, and Reopen for Done.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Requests exist in Open, In progress, and Done statuses. when The user opens each request detail screen. then The screen shows Start work, Mark done, and Reopen for the corresponding statuses.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a status change succeeds or fails, the request detail screen shall show the new status and corresponding action only after success, or show “Could not update the request.” while retaining the prior status after failure.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A request detail screen shows its current status and action button. when The user activates the button and the status API call succeeds. then After the response, the screen displays the new status badge and the corresponding next action button.\",\n    \"Given A request detail screen shows its current status and action button. when The user activates the button and the status API call fails. then The screen displays “Could not update the request.” and retains the prior status badge.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a request ID does not exist, the request detail screen shall display “Request not found.” and a link back to the Requests screen.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given No request has the ID in the address. when The user opens the detail screen for that ID. then The screen displays “Request not found.” and a link back to the Requests screen.\",\n    \"Given No request has the requested ID. when A client gets that ID through the API. then The response identifies the request as not found.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The maintenance request screens shall use one light theme, one sans-serif font, a neutral background, near-black text, and the specified status and priority badge colors with text labels on every badge.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The Requests and request detail screens are displayed. when A person inspects the theme and badges. then The screens show a light theme, sans-serif text, neutral background, near-black text, Open blue, In progress amber, Done green, Urgent red, Low and Normal neutral, and readable text on every badge.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The maintenance request screens shall show request dates as date-only values, use stacked cards at 375 px and table rows at 1280 px, avoid horizontal page scrolling at those widths, label every field, and make every control keyboard reachable with WCAG AA text contrast.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The Requests and detail screens are available. when A person inspects created dates and tests the screens at 375 px and 1280 px, including keyboard navigation and contrast. then The screen dates contain no time, the Requests list uses cards at 375 px and table rows at 1280 px, neither screen has horizontal page scroll, every field has a label, every control is keyboard reachable, and text meets WCAG AA contrast.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The maintenance request system shall display created dates as date-only values such as “8 Oct 2026” without a time or timezone.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A request has a stored UTC creation time. when The Requests list or detail screen displays that request. then The screen shows a date-only value such as “8 Oct 2026” with no time or timezone.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The maintenance request application shall include automated tests for the request business rules and an end-to-end list-to-completion workflow.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The automated business-rule test suite is available. when The test job runs. then The test run status is passed and its result list includes valid creation with Open status, missing and too-short title rejection, missing area rejection, too-long description rejection, all three allowed transitions, rejection of a disallowed transition, filtered newest-first listing, and unknown-ID not-found behavior.\",\n    \"Given The end-to-end test suite is available. when The end-to-end test job runs the list, create, open, Start work, Mark done, and Done-filter workflow. then The test run status is passed and its result list shows the created request at the top, then in the Done-filtered list after completion.\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  \"The Requests list shall adapt its layout for narrow and wide viewports without horizontal page scrolling.\",\n  \"Text shall meet WCAG AA contrast requirements.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nRestate the change."}